// A MATRIX entry parameter's default, on BOTH surfaces (t_4b54f26b A1).
//
// A1's first version accepted this shape and discarded the value: the
// parameter table read correctly and every row's ucode INLINE CONSTANT was
// zero, so an unpatched shader multiplied by a zero matrix. That is the same
// failure A3 fixed for FILE-SCOPE matrices, reproduced one branch over -
// the seeding sat in the general uniform branch, which a matrix entry
// parameter never reaches because an earlier branch builds its MatrixValue.
// Found by codex building the tree rather than reading the diff.
//
// Measured on the reference: rows at 336/368/400 in the table AND
// [1,2,3,0] / [4,5,6,0] / [7,8,9,0] in the ucode. The parent keeps defOff 0.
float4 main(float3 n : TEXCOORD0,
            uniform float3x3 M = float3x3(1,2,3, 4,5,6, 7,8,9)) : COLOR
{
	return float4(mul(M, n), 1.0);
}
